From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:35:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Performance metrics: composer, per-reply history

Stats for nerds turn performance in the web UI, coded against the
OrchestrationV2TurnPerformance contract.

- TurnPerformance.logic.ts: one provider turn -> metric rows (ttft, ttfa,
  liveTps, avgTps, peakTps, tokens, cache hit rate, context, tool time,
  turn time, provider, model, effort, speed), each exact / estimated /
  unavailable with a tooltip reason. avgTps uses generation windows only
  (exact only for provider_exact), legacy responseThroughput only under
  its own label. Client-side live tokens/s sampler (2 s window, keyed by
  thread + provider turn).
- Composer: one footer line while it fits, usage limits on the left and
  the running turn (elapsed, live tok/s, TTFT/TTFA), the previous
  completed turn and context on the right, each with a full breakdown on
  hover. Each side is a clipped line in priority order, so a narrow
  window drops the lowest-priority items before the right side wraps.
  The stats line hands its tok/s and cache chips to the turn summaries
  when they are shown.
- Timeline: the provider turn that produced each reply, right-aligned on
  the reply's action row (copy, fork, reply, time), with the breakdown on
  hover. It stays visible when the actions fade out and drops metrics in
  the composer's priority order instead of wrapping.
- Details: a compact grid instead of one row per metric. The provider
  icon, model, effort and speed head it as badges; short labels from the
  catalog (TTFT, Avg, Out, Hit%, ...) group timing, speed and tokens in
  three columns with compact numbers (332k, 1.8k); context is one bar.
  Each cell opens its full name, exact value and how it was measured on
  hover, click, tap or keyboard.
- Both follow the composer and per-reply settings and the hidden metric
  list (all shown by default). New catalog keys in every web locale.
